---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy | VT Analyzer";
const description = "How VT Analyzer collects, uses, and protects your data when you use our YouTube thumbnail analyzer.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} path="/privacy-policy/">
  <section class="bg-void py-14 text-mist">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5">
      <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mist/50">Last updated: July 1, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-10 px-5 py-16 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70 dark:text-smoke sm:text-base">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-sm border border-ink/10 dark:border-seam bg-paper-dim dark:bg-night-dim p-4 text-center">
        <p class="font-display text-sm font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">No Data Selling</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-ink/50 dark:text-smoke">We never sell personal information.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-sm border border-ink/10 dark:border-seam bg-paper-dim dark:bg-night-dim p-4 text-center">
        <p class="font-display text-sm font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Local-First Analysis</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-ink/50 dark:text-smoke">Uploaded images are processed in your browser.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-sm border border-ink/10 dark:border-seam bg-paper-dim dark:bg-night-dim p-4 text-center">
        <p class="font-display text-sm font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Transparency</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-ink/50 dark:text-smoke">Plain-language explanations, no legal jargon maze.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Introduction</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        This Privacy Policy explains how VT Analyzer ("we," "us") collects, uses, and safeguards
        information when you use our YouTube thumbnail analyzer at vtanalyzer.site (the "Service").
        By using the Service, you agree to the practices described here.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Information We Collect</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">We keep data collection to the minimum needed to operate the Service:</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li><strong>Thumbnail images.</strong> When you upload a file, the analysis happens directly in your browser using canvas image processing — the file is not transmitted to our servers. When you paste an image URL, your browser fetches that image directly from its source.</li>
        <li><strong>Contact information.</strong> If you email us or use the contact form, we receive whatever you choose to share — typically your name, email address, and message.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage analytics.</strong> We use standard, privacy-respecting analytics (such as aggregated page-view data) to understand how the Service is used and to improve it. This data is not tied to your uploaded images.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">How We Use Information</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>To provide, operate, and improve the thumbnail analyzer.</li>
        <li>To respond to support requests, feedback, and partnership inquiries.</li>
        <li>To understand aggregate usage patterns so we can prioritize improvements.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Cookies &amp; Similar Technologies</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We may use essential cookies or local storage to remember basic preferences, such as your
        selected color theme. These do not track you across other websites.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We may rely on third-party providers for hosting, analytics, or advertising. These
        providers may set their own cookies subject to their own privacy policies. We recommend
        reviewing the privacy policy of any third-party service linked from this site.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Data Retention</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Because thumbnail analysis happens locally in your browser, we do not retain a copy of
        your uploaded images. Contact form submissions are retained only as long as needed to
        respond to your inquiry, after which they are periodically deleted from our records.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Data Security</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect any information we do
        collect from unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. Because thumbnail
        analysis runs client-side in your browser, the images you check never traverse our network
        in the first place, which meaningfully reduces exposure. That said, no method of electronic
        storage or transmission is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security for
        any information transmitted to us, such as a contact form submission.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Advertising</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We may display advertising served by third-party advertising networks, such as Google
        AdSense. These networks may use cookies, web beacons, or similar technologies to collect
        information about your visits to this and other websites in order to provide relevant
        advertisements. This processing is governed by the respective advertising network's own
        privacy policy. You can learn more about how Google uses data when you use partner sites at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-red underline underline-offset-2">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>,
        and you can opt out of personalized advertising through
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-red underline underline-offset-2">Google's Ads Settings</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">International Data Transfers</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        VT Analyzer operates from India and may work with service providers located in other
        countries. If you access the Service from outside India, any information you voluntarily
        submit (such as a contact form message) may be processed in a country with different data
        protection laws than your own. By using the Service, you consent to this transfer and
        processing.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Do Not Track Signals</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Some browsers offer a "Do Not Track" setting. Because there is no common industry standard
        for how to interpret this signal, our Service does not currently alter its data collection
        practices when a Do Not Track signal is received.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Your Rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, update, port, or delete
        personal data we hold about you, and to object to or restrict certain processing. If you
        are located in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or a U.S. state with a
        comprehensive privacy law, additional rights may apply to you under GDPR, UK GDPR, or the
        relevant state statute. To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
        <a href="mailto:contact.vtanalyzer@gmail.com" class="text-red underline underline-offset-2">contact.vtanalyzer@gmail.com</a>
        and we will respond within a reasonable timeframe.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        The Service is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
        information from children. If we learn that we have inadvertently collected personal
        information from a child under 13, we will take steps to delete it as soon as reasonably
        possible. Parents or guardians who believe their child has provided us with information may
        contact us to request deletion.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by
        updating the "Last updated" date at the top of this page.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Contact Us</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Questions about this policy? Email
        <a href="mailto:contact.vtanalyzer@gmail.com" class="text-red underline underline-offset-2">contact.vtanalyzer@gmail.com</a>
        or visit our <a href="/contact/" class="text-red underline underline-offset-2">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
